Content:
HEADS UP:
Labels like FREE RANGE, CAGE FREE, and ALL NATURAL, can be incredibly misleading. They can be obtained by giving them the bare minimum. Cage Free can mean that they're just overcramped in a barn, All Natural is a bullshit label, and Free Range will almost always be exploited, as it doesn't specify roaming space, only the outdoor access factor, resulting in chickens or other animals usually being given minimal roaming space. Always look for Pasture Raised and Certified Humane

Sources:
@LawByMike (My Goat)
@ThoseAnnoyingVegans,
""Free Range" and "Pasture Raised" Officially Defined By HFAC For Certified Humane® Label ~ Humane Farm Animal Care Jan 16, 2014, 11:26 ET" from PR Newswire

